---Patch configuration specifications. Contains details on how to apply the patch(es) to a VM instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchConfig
---@field skipUnpatchableVms? boolean Optional. Enables enhanced reporting for the patch job: 1. The patch job skips instances that cannot be patched and reports them as `SKIPPED`. An instance cannot be patched for two reasons: 1. The instance runs Container-Optimized OS (COS), which cannot be patched. 2. The instance is part of a managed instance group (MIG), and patching MIG instances is disabled in the patch job's configuration (PatchConfig.migInstancesAllowed is `false`). 2. The patch job is reported as `SUCCEEDED` if it completes without errors, even if some instances are `SKIPPED`. 3. The patch job is reported as `COMPLETED_WITH_INACTIVE_VMS` if it completes without errors, but does not patch instances that are `INACTIVE`.
---@field zypper? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.ZypperSettings Zypper update settings. Use this setting to override the default `zypper` patch rules.
---@field apt? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.AptSettings Apt update settings. Use this setting to override the default `apt` patch rules.
---@field windowsUpdate? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.WindowsUpdateSettings Windows update settings. Use this override the default windows patch rules.
---@field preStep? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.ExecStep The `ExecStep` to run before the patch update.
---@field rebootConfig? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchConfigRebootConfigEnum|string Post-patch reboot settings.
---@field migInstancesAllowed? boolean Allows the patch job to run on Managed instance groups (MIGs).
---@field yum? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.YumSettings Yum update settings. Use this setting to override the default `yum` patch rules.
---@field postStep? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.ExecStep The `ExecStep` to run after the patch update.
---@field goo? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.GooSettings Goo update settings. Use this setting to override the default `goo` patch rules.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchConfigRebootConfigEnum "REBOOT_CONFIG_UNSPECIFIED"|"DEFAULT"|"ALWAYS"|"NEVER"

---Patch deployments are configurations that individual patch jobs use to complete a patch. These configurations include instance filter, package repository settings, and a schedule. For more information about creating and managing patch deployments, see [Scheduling patch jobs](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/os-patch-management/schedule-patch-jobs).
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchDeployment
---@field instanceFilter? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchInstanceFilter Required. VM instances to patch.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time the patch deployment was created. Timestamp is in [RFC3339](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3339.txt) text format.
