---A filter to target VM instances for patching. The targeted VMs must meet all criteria specified. So if both labels and zones are specified, the patch job targets only VMs with those labels and in those zones.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchInstanceFilter
---@field all? boolean Target all VM instances in the project. If true, no other criteria is permitted.
---@field groupLabels? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchInstanceFilterGroupLabelList Targets VM instances matching at least one of these label sets. This allows targeting of disparate groups, for example "env=prod or env=staging".
---@field instanceNamePrefixes? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList Targets VMs whose name starts with one of these prefixes. Similar to labels, this is another way to group VMs when targeting configs, for example prefix="prod-".
---@field zones? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList Targets VM instances in ANY of these zones. Leave empty to target VM instances in any zone.
---@field instances? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList Targets any of the VM instances specified. Instances are specified by their URI in the form `zones/[ZONE]/instances/[INSTANCE_NAME]`, `projects/[PROJECT_ID]/zones/[ZONE]/instances/[INSTANCE_NAME]`, or `https://www.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/[PROJECT_ID]/zones/[ZONE]/instances/[INSTANCE_NAME]`

---Represents a group of VMs that can be identified as having all these labels, for example "env=prod and app=web".
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchInstanceFilterGroupLabel
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringMap Compute Engine instance labels that must be present for a VM instance to be targeted by this filter.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchInstanceFilterGroupLabelList gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchInstanceFilterGroupLabel[]

---A high level representation of a patch job that is either in progress or has completed. Instance details are not included in the job. To paginate through instance details, use `ListPatchJobInstanceDetails`. For more information about patch jobs, see [Creating patch jobs](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/os-patch-management/create-patch-job).
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchJob
---@field percentComplete? number Reflects the overall progress of the patch job in the range of 0.0 being no progress to 100.0 being complete.
---@field patchDeployment? string Output only. Name of the patch deployment that created this patch job.
---@field instanceFilter? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchInstanceFilter Instances to patch.
---@field patchConfig? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchConfig Patch configuration being applied.
---@field name? string Unique identifier for this patch job in the form `projects/*/patchJobs/*`
---@field createTime? string Time this patch job was created.
---@field instanceDetailsSummary? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchJobInstanceDetailsSummary Summary of instance details.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchJobStateEnum The current state of the PatchJob.
---@field updateTime? string Last time this patch job was updated.
---@field rollout? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchRollout Rollout strategy being applied.
---@field dryRun? boolean If this patch job is a dry run, the agent reports that it has finished without running any updates on the VM instance.
---@field displayName? string Display name for this patch job. This is not a unique identifier.
---@field errorMessage? string If this patch job failed, this message provides information about the failure.
---@field description? string Description of the patch job. Length of the description is limited to 1024 characters.
---@field duration? string Duration of the patch job. After the duration ends, the patch job times out.

---Patch details for a VM instance. For more information about reviewing VM instance details, see [Listing all VM instance details for a specific patch job](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/os-patch-management/manage-patch-jobs#list-instance-details).
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchJobInstanceDetails
---@field failureReason? string If the patch fails, this field provides the reason.
---@field instanceSystemId? string The unique identifier for the instance. This identifier is defined by the server.
---@field attemptCount? string The number of times the agent that the agent attempts to apply the patch.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchJobInstanceDetailsStateEnum Current state of instance patch.
---@field name? string The instance name in the form `projects/*/zones/*/instances/*`

