---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchProjectsGuestPoliciesRequest
---@field etag? string The etag for this guest policy. If this is provided on update, it must match the server's etag.
---@field assignment? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.Assignment Required. Specifies the VM instances that are assigned to this policy. This allows you to target sets or groups of VM instances by different parameters such as labels, names, OS, or zones. If left empty, all VM instances underneath this policy are targeted. At the same level in the resource hierarchy (that is within a project), the service prevents the creation of multiple policies that conflict with each other. For more information, see how the service [handles assignment conflicts](/compute/docs/os-config-management/create-guest-policy#handle-conflicts).
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Last time this guest policy was updated.
---@field recipes? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeList A list of Recipes to install on the VM instance.
---@field packages? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PackageList The software packages to be managed by this policy.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time this guest policy was created.
---@field description? string Description of the guest policy. Length of the description is limited to 1024 characters.
---@field packageRepositories? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PackageRepositoryList A list of package repositories to configure on the VM instance. This is done before any other configs are applied so they can use these repos. Package repositories are only configured if the corresponding package manager(s) are available.
---@field updateMask? string Field mask that controls which fields of the guest policy should be updated.
---@field name string Required. Unique name of the resource in this project using one of the following forms: `projects/{project_number}/guestPolicies/{guest_policy_id}`.

---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchProjectsPatchDeploymentsRequest
---@field instanceFilter? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchInstanceFilter Required. VM instances to patch.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time the patch deployment was created. Timestamp is in [RFC3339](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3339.txt) text format.
---@field oneTimeSchedule? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.OneTimeSchedule Required. Schedule a one-time execution.
---@field description? string Optional. Description of the patch deployment. Length of the description is limited to 1024 characters.
---@field duration? string Optional. Duration of the patch. After the duration ends, the patch times out.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchDeploymentStateEnum|string Output only. Current state of the patch deployment.
---@field patchConfig? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchConfig Optional. Patch configuration that is applied.
---@field lastExecuteTime? string Output only. The last time a patch job was started by this deployment. Timestamp is in [RFC3339](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3339.txt) text format.
---@field rollout? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchRollout Optional. Rollout strategy of the patch job.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time the patch deployment was last updated. Timestamp is in [RFC3339](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3339.txt) text format.
---@field recurringSchedule? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.RecurringSchedule Required. Schedule recurring executions.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. Field mask that controls which fields of the patch deployment should be updated.
---@field name string Unique name for the patch deployment resource in a project. The patch deployment name is in the form: `projects/{project_id}/patchDeployments/{patch_deployment_id}`. This field is ignored when you create a new patch deployment.

---Patch rollout configuration specifications. Contains details on the concurrency control when applying patch(es) to all targeted VMs.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchRollout
---@field mode? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchRolloutModeEnum|string Mode of the patch rollout.
---@field disruptionBudget? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.FixedOrPercent The maximum number (or percentage) of VMs per zone to disrupt at any given moment. The number of VMs calculated from multiplying the percentage by the total number of VMs in a zone is rounded up. During patching, a VM is considered disrupted from the time the agent is notified to begin until patching has completed. This disruption time includes the time to complete reboot and any post-patch steps. A VM contributes to the disruption budget if its patching operation fails either when applying the patches, running pre or post patch steps, or if it fails to respond with a success notification before timing out. VMs that are not running or do not have an active agent do not count toward this disruption budget. For zone-by-zone rollouts, if the disruption budget in a zone is exceeded, the patch job stops, because continuing to the next zone requires completion of the patch process in the previous zone. For example, if the disruption budget has a fixed value of `10`, and 8 VMs fail to patch in the current zone, the patch job continues to patch 2 VMs at a time until the zone is completed. When that zone is completed successfully, patching begins with 10 VMs at a time in the next zone. If 10 VMs in the next zone fail to patch, the patch job stops.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.PatchRolloutModeEnum "MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ZONE_BY_ZONE"|"CONCURRENT_ZONES"

