---A software recipe is a set of instructions for installing and configuring a piece of software. It consists of a set of artifacts that are downloaded, and a set of steps that install, configure, and/or update the software. Recipes support installing and updating software from artifacts in the following formats: Zip archive, Tar archive, Windows MSI, Debian package, and RPM package. Additionally, recipes support executing a script (either defined in a file or directly in this api) in bash, sh, cmd, and powershell. Updating a software recipe If a recipe is assigned to an instance and there is a recipe with the same name but a lower version already installed and the assigned state of the recipe is `UPDATED`, then the recipe is updated to the new version. Script Working Directories Each script or execution step is run in its own temporary directory which is deleted after completing the step.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipe
---@field installSteps? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepList Actions to be taken for installing this recipe. On failure it stops executing steps and does not attempt another installation. Any steps taken (including partially completed steps) are not rolled back.
---@field name? string Required. Unique identifier for the recipe. Only one recipe with a given name is installed on an instance. Names are also used to identify resources which helps to determine whether guest policies have conflicts. This means that requests to create multiple recipes with the same name and version are rejected since they could potentially have conflicting assignments.
---@field desiredState? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeDesiredStateEnum|string Default is INSTALLED. The desired state the agent should maintain for this recipe. INSTALLED: The software recipe is installed on the instance but won't be updated to new versions. UPDATED: The software recipe is installed on the instance. The recipe is updated to a higher version, if a higher version of the recipe is assigned to this instance. REMOVE: Remove is unsupported for software recipes and attempts to create or update a recipe to the REMOVE state is rejected.
---@field updateSteps? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepList Actions to be taken for updating this recipe. On failure it stops executing steps and does not attempt another update for this recipe. Any steps taken (including partially completed steps) are not rolled back.
---@field artifacts? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeArtifactList Resources available to be used in the steps in the recipe.
---@field version? string The version of this software recipe. Version can be up to 4 period separated numbers (e.g. 12.34.56.78).

---Specifies a resource to be used in the recipe.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeArtifact
---@field id? string Required. Id of the artifact, which the installation and update steps of this recipe can reference. Artifacts in a recipe cannot have the same id.
---@field allowInsecure? boolean Defaults to false. When false, recipes are subject to validations based on the artifact type: Remote: A checksum must be specified, and only protocols with transport-layer security are permitted. GCS: An object generation number must be specified.
---@field remote? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeArtifactRemote A generic remote artifact.
---@field gcs? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeArtifactGcs A Google Cloud Storage artifact.

---Specifies an artifact available as a Google Cloud Storage object.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeArtifactGcs
---@field bucket? string Bucket of the Google Cloud Storage object. Given an example URL: `https://storage.googleapis.com/my-bucket/foo/bar#1234567` this value would be `my-bucket`.
---@field object? string Name of the Google Cloud Storage object. As specified [here] (https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/naming#objectnames) Given an example URL: `https://storage.googleapis.com/my-bucket/foo/bar#1234567` this value would be `foo/bar`.
---@field generation? string Must be provided if allow_insecure is false. Generation number of the Google Cloud Storage object. `https://storage.googleapis.com/my-bucket/foo/bar#1234567` this value would be `1234567`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeArtifactList gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeArtifact[]

---Specifies an artifact available via some URI.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeArtifactRemote
---@field uri? string URI from which to fetch the object. It should contain both the protocol and path following the format {protocol}://{location}.
---@field checksum? string Must be provided if `allow_insecure` is `false`. SHA256 checksum in hex format, to compare to the checksum of the artifact. If the checksum is not empty and it doesn't match the artifact then the recipe installation fails before running any of the steps.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeDesiredStateEnum "DESIRED_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"INSTALLED"|"UPDATED"|"REMOVED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeList gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipe[]

---An action that can be taken as part of installing or updating a recipe.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStep
---@field scriptRun? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepRunScript Runs commands in a shell.
---@field dpkgInstallation? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepInstallDpkg Installs a deb file via dpkg.
---@field rpmInstallation? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepInstallRpm Installs an rpm file via the rpm utility.
---@field fileCopy? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepCopyFile Copies a file onto the instance.
---@field archiveExtraction? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepExtractArchive Extracts an archive into the specified directory.
---@field msiInstallation? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepInstallMsi Installs an MSI file.
---@field fileExec? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepExecFile Executes an artifact or local file.

---Copies the artifact to the specified path on the instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepCopyFile
---@field artifactId? string Required. The id of the relevant artifact in the recipe.
---@field overwrite? boolean Whether to allow this step to overwrite existing files. If this is false and the file already exists the file is not overwritten and the step is considered a success. Defaults to false.
---@field permissions? string Consists of three octal digits which represent, in order, the permissions of the owner, group, and other users for the file (similarly to the numeric mode used in the linux chmod utility). Each digit represents a three bit number with the 4 bit corresponding to the read permissions, the 2 bit corresponds to the write bit, and the one bit corresponds to the execute permission. Default behavior is 755. Below are some examples of permissions and their associated values: read, write, and execute: 7 read and execute: 5 read and write: 6 read only: 4
---@field destination? string Required. The absolute path on the instance to put the file.

---Executes an artifact or local file.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepExecFile
---@field args? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList Arguments to be passed to the provided executable.
---@field localPath? string The absolute path of the file on the local filesystem.
---@field allowedExitCodes? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.IntegerList Defaults to [0]. A list of possible return values that the program can return to indicate a success.
---@field artifactId? string The id of the relevant artifact in the recipe.

---Extracts an archive of the type specified in the specified directory.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepExtractArchive
---@field artifactId? string Required. The id of the relevant artifact in the recipe.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepExtractArchiveTypeEnum|string Required. The type of the archive to extract.
---@field destination? string Directory to extract archive to. Defaults to `/` on Linux or `C:\` on Windows.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepExtractArchiveTypeEnum "ARCHIVE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"TAR"|"TAR_GZIP"|"TAR_BZIP"|"TAR_LZMA"|"TAR_XZ"|"ZIP"

---Installs a deb via dpkg.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepInstallDpkg
---@field artifactId? string Required. The id of the relevant artifact in the recipe.

---Installs an MSI file.
