---@field allowedExitCodes? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.IntegerList Return codes that indicate that the software installed or updated successfully. Behaviour defaults to [0]
---@field flags? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList The flags to use when installing the MSI defaults to ["/i"] (i.e. the install flag).
---@field artifactId? string Required. The id of the relevant artifact in the recipe.

---Installs an rpm file via the rpm utility.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepInstallRpm
---@field artifactId? string Required. The id of the relevant artifact in the recipe.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepList gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStep[]

---Runs a script through an interpreter.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepRunScript
---@field interpreter? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepRunScriptInterpreterEnum|string The script interpreter to use to run the script. If no interpreter is specified the script is executed directly, which likely only succeed for scripts with [shebang lines](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shebang_\(Unix\)).
---@field allowedExitCodes? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.IntegerList Return codes that indicate that the software installed or updated successfully. Behaviour defaults to [0]
---@field script? string Required. The shell script to be executed.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.SoftwareRecipeStepRunScriptInterpreterEnum "INTERPRETER_UNSPECIFIED"|"SHELL"|"POWERSHELL"

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList string[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringMap { [string]: string }

---Represents a time of day. The date and time zone are either not significant or are specified elsewhere. An API may choose to allow leap seconds. Related types are google.type.Date and `google.protobuf.Timestamp`.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.TimeOfDay
---@field hours? number Hours of a day in 24 hour format. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and typically must be less than or equal to 23. An API may choose to allow the value "24:00:00" for scenarios like business closing time.
---@field nanos? number Fractions of seconds, in nanoseconds. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to 999,999,999.
---@field seconds? number Seconds of a minute. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and typically must be less than or equal to 59. An API may allow the value 60 if it allows leap-seconds.
---@field minutes? number Minutes of an hour. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to 59.

---Represents a time zone from the [IANA Time Zone Database](https://www.iana.org/time-zones).
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.TimeZone
---@field id? string IANA Time Zone Database time zone. For example "America/New_York".
---@field version? string Optional. IANA Time Zone Database version number. For example "2019a".

---Represents one week day in a month. An example is "the 4th Sunday".
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.WeekDayOfMonth
---@field weekOrdinal? number Required. Week number in a month. 1-4 indicates the 1st to 4th week of the month. -1 indicates the last week of the month.
---@field dayOfWeek? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.WeekDayOfMonthDayOfWeekEnum|string Required. A day of the week.
---@field dayOffset? number Optional. Represents the number of days before or after the given week day of month that the patch deployment is scheduled for. For example if `week_ordinal` and `day_of_week` values point to the second day of the month and this `day_offset` value is set to `3`, the patch deployment takes place three days after the second Tuesday of the month. If this value is negative, for example -5, the patches are deployed five days before before the second Tuesday of the month. Allowed values are in range [-30, 30].

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.WeekDayOfMonthDayOfWeekEnum "DAY_OF_WEEK_UNSPECIFIED"|"MONDAY"|"TUESDAY"|"WEDNESDAY"|"THURSDAY"|"FRIDAY"|"SATURDAY"|"SUNDAY"

---Represents a weekly schedule.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.WeeklySchedule
---@field dayOfWeek? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.WeeklyScheduleDayOfWeekEnum|string Required. Day of the week.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.WeeklyScheduleDayOfWeekEnum "DAY_OF_WEEK_UNSPECIFIED"|"MONDAY"|"TUESDAY"|"WEDNESDAY"|"THURSDAY"|"FRIDAY"|"SATURDAY"|"SUNDAY"

---Windows patching is performed using the Windows Update Agent.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.WindowsUpdateSettings
---@field exclusivePatches? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList An exclusive list of kbs to be updated. These are the only patches that will be updated. This field must not be used with other patch configurations.
---@field excludes? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList List of KBs to exclude from update.
