---Represents a single Yum package repository. This repository is added to a repo file that is stored at `/etc/yum.repos.d/google_osconfig.repo`.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.YumRepository
---@field baseUrl? string Required. The location of the repository directory.
---@field displayName? string The display name of the repository.
---@field id? string Required. A one word, unique name for this repository. This is the `repo id` in the Yum config file and also the `display_name` if `display_name` is omitted. This id is also used as the unique identifier when checking for guest policy conflicts.
---@field gpgKeys? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList URIs of GPG keys.

---Yum patching is performed by executing `yum update`. Additional options can be set to control how this is executed. Note that not all settings are supported on all platforms.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.YumSettings
---@field security? boolean Adds the `--security` flag to `yum update`. Not supported on all platforms.
---@field excludes? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList List of packages to exclude from update. These packages are excluded by using the yum `--exclude` flag.
---@field exclusivePackages? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList An exclusive list of packages to be updated. These are the only packages that will be updated. If these packages are not installed, they will be ignored. This field must not be specified with any other patch configuration fields.
---@field minimal? boolean Will cause patch to run `yum update-minimal` instead.

---Represents a single Zypper package repository. This repository is added to a repo file that is stored at `/etc/zypp/repos.d/google_osconfig.repo`.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.ZypperRepository
---@field id? string Required. A one word, unique name for this repository. This is the `repo id` in the zypper config file and also the `display_name` if `display_name` is omitted. This id is also used as the unique identifier when checking for guest policy conflicts.
---@field gpgKeys? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList URIs of GPG keys.
---@field baseUrl? string Required. The location of the repository directory.
---@field displayName? string The display name of the repository.

---Zypper patching is performed by running `zypper patch`. See also https://en.opensuse.org/SDB:Zypper_manual.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.ZypperSettings
---@field categories? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList Install only patches with these categories. Common categories include security, recommended, and feature.
---@field exclusivePatches? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList An exclusive list of patches to be updated. These are the only patches that will be installed using 'zypper patch patch:' command. This field must not be used with any other patch configuration fields.
---@field withOptional? boolean Adds the `--with-optional` flag to `zypper patch`.
---@field excludes? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList List of patches to exclude from update.
---@field withUpdate? boolean Adds the `--with-update` flag, to `zypper patch`.
---@field severities? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1beta.StringList Install only patches with these severities. Common severities include critical, important, moderate, and low.

